Package: scStable
Type: Package
Title: Assessing scRNA-seq analysis stability under bulk-derived sample variation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Chengfeng",
           family = "Jiang",
           email = "cfjiang@ucla.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: scStable generates synthetic single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq)
    replicates from a single input scRNA-seq sample by injecting realistic
    between-sample variation learned from multi-sample bulk RNA-seq data while
    preserving cell-level heterogeneity. The bulk reference can be provided by
    the user or obtained from tissue-matched public resources such as GTEx.
    The resulting synthetic samples enable stability-aware scRNA-seq analysis,
    including quantifying the stability of discoveries such as differentially
    expressed genes and stress-testing analysis methods under different levels
    of injected variation. By evaluating the consistency of results across
    synthetic samples, scStable supports stability-driven methods and
    hyperparameters selection.
